WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:03.780
I have to ask you a few questions about Solskjær.

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:05.980
Because I am, after all, Norwegian.

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:07.600
I understand.

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:09.260
As you might have understood.

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:13.560
So Ole Gunnar Solskjær has become ...

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:17.240
... and interim manager for your team.

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:18.600
Exactly.

00:00:18.700 --> 00:00:21.340
He has done quite well.

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:24.400
He has won most of the matches.

00:00:24.580 --> 00:00:26.920
He has come in with a very nice energy and ...

00:00:26.920 --> 00:00:31.540
... he has really made the team believe in the football that he wants to play and ...

00:00:31.540 --> 00:00:34.540
... also that we should believe in ourselves and in our qualities.

00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:37.040
I think he has done a really good job since he came in.

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:40.260
Is that something that you've missed in this team?

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:43.000
That feeling?

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:46.840
Eeeeeehhh.

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:48.520
Careful, now!

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:54.340
I'm not sure what to answer to that.

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:58.900
I only want to praise Ole, I think that he's done a very good job since he came in and ...

00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:02.220
I know that a lot of people like him and think that he's handled ...

00:01:02.220 --> 00:01:05.840
... all the players well since he came there.

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:06.900
That's what I can say.

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:07.960
Yeah, yeah, but ...

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:08.680
If you ...

00:01:08.880 --> 00:01:09.660
Let's just say ...

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:12.300
If you owned the team, if it was your team ...

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:13.880
Would you hire him then?

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:17.780
I guess you have to say that!

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:21.480
I've been sitting here praising him, and I think he's done a fantastic job.

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:23.980
But it's not up to me to sit here and answer that.

00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:25.120
I don't think so.

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:27.860
But as I said, he's done a very good job.

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:28.720
He's hired!

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:30.580
You're hired!

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:34.440
How wonderful!

00:01:34.540 --> 00:01:35.040
Yes.

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:36.020
Fun to be here!

00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:38.020
You've driven down from Manchester.

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:38.920
Yes.

00:01:38.920 --> 00:01:41.820
I forced him. He doesn't like interviews and stuff like that.

00:01:41.960 --> 00:01:45.320
But I told him: «Skavlan! You don't say no to that!»

00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:47.820
It's actually true.

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:49.440
It's thanks to me we're sitting here!

00:01:49.940 --> 00:01:52.560
And you can tell that to the rest of your team, as well!

00:01:52.800 --> 00:01:55.580
I'll do my best. I can't make any promises, but I'll do my best!

00:01:56.480 --> 00:02:00.360
Firstly, Börje and I have been talking ...

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:03.860
... not about football, but about proposals.

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:09.860
How spontaneous was it when you, I don't know which one of you did it, proposed?

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:12.020
I was the one who proposed.

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:14.400
Was it well planned, or was it ...

00:02:14.740 --> 00:02:16.180
It was quite planned.

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:20.960
I thought about ... Or, I spent six or seven months planning it.

00:02:20.960 --> 00:02:21.480
Maybe.

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:22.280
That's quite long!

00:02:23.260 --> 00:02:25.340
That was a very long time, actually!

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:28.700
But it takes a while finding the ring and things like that, and you want it to be good!

00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:29.440
So ...

00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:32.100
Yes. I found a nice ring.

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:35.900
And then we traveled to the Maldives, Maja and I, and then ...

00:02:36.440 --> 00:02:37.400
I had fixed ...

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:39.160
Did you feel that «it's happening now»?

00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:39.920
No.

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:41.840
I've always wanted to get married.

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:44.440
And he has been like: «I don't want to get married».

00:02:44.500 --> 00:02:46.440
So I had actually accepted that.

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:47.660
And thought that we wouldn't get married.

00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:49.340
I was playing a game there! I tricked her a little.

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:54.680
So I had no idea. And he did it the third day of our journey.

00:02:54.680 --> 00:03:00.040
You would think that he would do it the first day. Or the last. The last is maybe a bit strange, but the first!

00:03:00.040 --> 00:03:01.400
But it was the third!

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:03.100
I had planned it perfectly, quite simply!

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:05.900
How had you set this up?

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:11.360
We were going to have a little picnic under the stars after dinner.

00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:12.520
Yeah.

00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:14.900
It was hard to fail with that. But ...

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:18.860
In the middle of dinner, we had maybe been there in ...

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:19.780
30-40 minutes.

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:20.840
Yes, it wasn't long.

00:03:21.560 --> 00:03:25.140
... the skies opened up and it just poured rain.

00:03:26.720 --> 00:03:31.600
And we were sitting underneath a tent made with sticks, not a real tent ...

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:34.060
So it just poured everywhere.

00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:36.860
And had he had time to ask the question, or ..?

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:37.360
No.

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:39.600
So I became very stressed there!

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:43.120
And I tried to play calm and ...

00:03:43.580 --> 00:03:48.080
«It doesn't matter, it's just a little rain, we can go back later.» But I think Maja noticed ...

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:49.540
... that I was quite stressed!

00:03:49.720 --> 00:03:50.920
Really stressed!

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:54.760
And I just said: «It's just a little rain»!

00:03:55.180 --> 00:03:58.920
But we then went to a restaurant that was nearby.

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:00.720
And we had a nice dinner.

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:04.840
And then we went down to the beach and ...

00:04:05.100 --> 00:04:06.680
And I popped the question!

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:09.680
Down on your knee?

00:04:09.760 --> 00:04:12.680
I went down on my knee. But I had ...

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:14.540
The ring is in a box.

00:04:14.540 --> 00:04:19.760
And I thought that I should bring the box, because I wanted to open it when I was down on my knee.

00:04:24.600 --> 00:04:28.580
But I didn't know where to put this box.

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:37.960
Because you can't have it in your pocket ...

00:04:37.960 --> 00:04:40.700
I was wearing shorts. It was in the Maldives.

00:04:40.700 --> 00:04:42.240
So ...

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:45.140
So I thought, «where should I put this box»?

00:04:45.980 --> 00:04:50.980
So right before we left, I stuffed it into my pants.

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:53.960
And I put it right here.

00:04:54.320 --> 00:04:57.540
So I had to walk like this!

00:04:58.360 --> 00:05:00.680
She didn't see anything, at least!

00:05:00.680 --> 00:05:01.760
So it worked out.

00:05:02.660 --> 00:05:06.680
So I just went behind a bush and pretended that I wanted to pee and then I took the box out.

00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:19.960
They call you «The Ice Man».

00:05:19.960 --> 00:05:20.580
Exactly.

00:05:20.680 --> 00:05:24.020
It doesn't feel like that. You're not very ...

00:05:24.020 --> 00:05:26.540
I actually don't know why I've gotten that nickname!

00:05:26.540 --> 00:05:29.660
Do you understand that, do you wake up with «The Ice Man» every morning?

00:05:29.660 --> 00:05:32.960
I think they're referring to how he seems on the outside.

00:05:32.960 --> 00:05:36.700
With the media and ... They rarely get anything out of you!

00:05:41.480 --> 00:05:43.640
I suppose it must come from that.

00:05:43.720 --> 00:05:44.660
I think.

00:05:44.660 --> 00:05:49.220
I think it's a mix of how I seem from the outside ...

00:05:49.220 --> 00:05:51.480
I'm quite a private person.

00:05:51.820 --> 00:05:54.300
I'm not very fond of sharing too much.

00:05:54.300 --> 00:05:56.620
And I also think it's because I'm quite calm on the field.

00:05:56.860 --> 00:05:59.820
So I think it's a mix of those two things.

00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:01.440
That you keep your cool?

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:02.220
Yes, exactly.

00:06:02.220 --> 00:06:06.080
Do you two have the same temper, or do you have different ones?

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:08.140
We're both heated.

00:06:08.160 --> 00:06:12.160
Yes! You now think that he doesn't have a temper, but he does!

00:06:12.160 --> 00:06:13.540
Yes, I think that «The Ice Man» sounds very calm!

00:06:13.540 --> 00:06:14.400
No, no, no!

00:06:14.680 --> 00:06:16.400
I can get very mad.

00:06:16.400 --> 00:06:18.300
There's a Börje Salming in there?

00:06:18.360 --> 00:06:19.280
Yes.

00:06:19.920 --> 00:06:22.220
I don't think I ... Well, I'm not so sure of that!

00:06:22.480 --> 00:06:24.560
He's at another level, I think!

00:06:24.560 --> 00:06:26.360
But I'm very calm now, so it's all good!

00:06:28.440 --> 00:06:32.700
Of course I can get mad, but I think that both Maja and I have a pretty heated temper sometimes.

00:06:33.080 --> 00:06:34.760
How much do you follow ...

00:06:34.760 --> 00:06:38.180
Your job is very modern, it's called an influencer.

00:06:38.180 --> 00:06:43.100
But you also do a podcast, and you have a blog, and you do different things in social media.

00:06:44.220 --> 00:06:48.780
You have moved to Manchester.

00:06:49.040 --> 00:06:52.140
And the two of you work with very different things.

00:06:52.140 --> 00:06:52.640
Yes.

00:06:52.640 --> 00:06:54.860
Do you keep up with each other's work?

00:06:55.620 --> 00:06:56.940
No.

00:06:58.360 --> 00:07:03.260
I support you, and you support me, but we're not ...

00:07:03.560 --> 00:07:06.640
... very ... I don't really want to have Victor in what I do.

00:07:07.320 --> 00:07:09.960
And he obviously doesn't want me in what he does.

00:07:09.960 --> 00:07:12.320
I go and watch matches and things like that, but ...

00:07:12.320 --> 00:07:14.720
He doesn't come home and talks football with me.

00:07:15.040 --> 00:07:20.640
For example, if she does a podcast, does she expect you to listen to all the episodes?

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:21.960
Oh yes.

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:23.760
I've heard that many times!

00:07:24.560 --> 00:07:27.120
I can admit that I haven't been very good at that.

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:29.620
No! Really bad!

00:07:29.700 --> 00:07:33.240
Yes. But he always reads everything I write.

00:07:33.960 --> 00:07:35.080
Things like that.

00:07:35.080 --> 00:07:35.580
I do.

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:39.540
Does it limit you that he plays in Manchester United?

00:07:39.780 --> 00:07:43.460
Yes. But it also benefits me, of course, I'm not stupid.

00:07:44.780 --> 00:07:47.340
I take advantage of that.

00:07:47.880 --> 00:07:50.440
But I think we've found a good balance.

00:07:50.440 --> 00:07:53.780
Before it was harder for me to know what I could and couldn't write.

00:07:53.940 --> 00:07:58.360
I could come home and just be like «ughhh», because there was something written in the news, and ...

00:07:58.360 --> 00:08:01.300
... and he would come home from training and I would just feel like ...

00:08:01.300 --> 00:08:04.460
... «I'm just gonna lock myself in here, because he's gonna wanna have a chat with me».

00:08:04.640 --> 00:08:07.120
But I've learnt now, for sure.

00:08:07.120 --> 00:08:09.700
There's a term called «footballer's wife».

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:13.600
I know that you don't like that term.

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:14.800
No.

00:08:14.800 --> 00:08:17.980
I think that it's degrading to women, quite simply.

00:08:17.980 --> 00:08:22.520
I am married to Victor and he plays football, and I understand that ...

00:08:22.640 --> 00:08:25.180
... it's easy to use that word.

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:30.000
But I still feel that there's something degrading in that word.

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:32.840
And that's why it provokes me, I think.

00:08:32.840 --> 00:08:36.460
I also think that people don't really ...

00:08:38.820 --> 00:08:44.340
People look down on it and think that the women just stay at home and do this and that.

00:08:44.340 --> 00:08:45.720
While he plays football.

00:08:45.720 --> 00:08:47.420
And they don't know anything.

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:51.960
Do you feel that you're ...

00:08:52.560 --> 00:08:56.640
... being looked at when you're on the stands watching a game?

00:08:56.740 --> 00:09:00.780
That people view you in a certain way and that they label you?

00:09:01.320 --> 00:09:04.140
That they place you somewhere?

00:09:04.140 --> 00:09:08.580
I used to think so before. But now I feel like I'm starting to become my own person.

00:09:08.580 --> 00:09:14.040
Today, when I wrote that I was going here, lots of people said that they would watch because I'm here, and not because he's here.

00:09:15.320 --> 00:09:17.640
I feel that I've arrived somewhere.

00:09:21.580 --> 00:09:25.620
I have to ask you a few questions about Solskjær.

00:09:25.620 --> 00:09:27.980
Because I am, after all, Norwegian.

00:09:28.420 --> 00:09:29.380
I understand.

00:09:29.380 --> 00:09:30.800
As you might have understood.

00:09:31.240 --> 00:09:35.080
So Ole Gunnar Solskjær has become ...

00:09:35.640 --> 00:09:38.740
... an interim manager for your team.

00:09:39.400 --> 00:09:40.240
Exactly.

00:09:40.400 --> 00:09:43.000
He has done quite well.

00:09:43.260 --> 00:09:46.020
He has won most of the matches.

00:09:46.020 --> 00:09:48.360
He has come in with a very nice energy and ...

00:09:48.360 --> 00:09:53.060
... he has really made the team believe in the football that he wants to play and ...

00:09:53.060 --> 00:09:55.920
... also that we should believe in ourselves and in our qualities.

00:09:55.920 --> 00:09:58.640
I think he has done a really good job since he came in.

00:09:58.640 --> 00:10:01.700
Is that something that you've missed in the team?

00:10:02.380 --> 00:10:04.880
That feeling?

00:10:07.460 --> 00:10:09.000
Eeeeeehhh.

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:11.000
Careful, now!

00:10:13.140 --> 00:10:15.460
I don't know what to answer to that.

00:10:16.520 --> 00:10:20.440
I only want to praise Ole, I think that he's done a very good job since he came in and ...

00:10:20.440 --> 00:10:23.820
I know that a lot of people like him and they way he's handled ...

00:10:24.020 --> 00:10:26.960
... the players since he came there.

00:10:26.960 --> 00:10:28.320
That's what I can say.

00:10:28.320 --> 00:10:29.400
Yeah, yeah, but ...

00:10:29.480 --> 00:10:33.760
Let's just say, if you owned the team, if it was your team ...

00:10:33.940 --> 00:10:35.220
Would you hire him?

00:10:38.240 --> 00:10:40.080
I guess you have to say that!

00:10:40.080 --> 00:10:42.840
I've been sitting here praising him, and I think he's done a fantastic job.

00:10:42.840 --> 00:10:45.560
But I don't think it's up to me to answer that.

00:10:45.580 --> 00:10:46.700
I don't think so.

00:10:47.440 --> 00:10:49.620
But as I said, I think he's done a really good job.

00:10:49.620 --> 00:10:50.420
He's hired!

00:10:50.660 --> 00:10:52.160
You're hired!

00:10:57.660 --> 00:11:00.020
I have to ask you how ...

00:11:01.080 --> 00:11:04.920
... a day in your life looks. Because you're living the dream, according to many.

00:11:05.480 --> 00:11:09.160
To be a professional football player, and be able to ...

00:11:09.160 --> 00:11:13.120
... buy a really expensive house, live in England and play for Manchester United.

00:11:13.120 --> 00:11:14.180
A lot of people have that dream.

00:11:14.180 --> 00:11:17.640
And to live the life that you do as well.

00:11:17.640 --> 00:11:20.240
But there is an everyday life for you as well.

00:11:20.760 --> 00:11:23.200
How «normal» is that?

00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:29.140
We have an everyday life, but none of us have that «it's Monday, it's seven in the morning» ...

00:11:29.620 --> 00:11:31.780
... «get up». We don't have that.

00:11:31.880 --> 00:11:34.520
And we understand that that is a luxury.

00:11:34.520 --> 00:11:36.240
Yeah. We don't have that Sunday anxiety.

00:11:36.240 --> 00:11:37.300
We really don't.

00:11:37.300 --> 00:11:38.780
And we appreciate that.

00:11:39.160 --> 00:11:43.120
So you don't get up at seven, when do you wake up, then?

00:11:44.420 --> 00:11:46.340
When I wake up every morning?

00:11:46.660 --> 00:11:47.620
When do I get up? Nine?

00:11:47.620 --> 00:11:49.280
Quarter to nine? I get up at ...

00:11:49.280 --> 00:11:50.860
You get up a nine?!

00:11:52.300 --> 00:11:53.860
I get up at nine.

00:11:53.860 --> 00:11:57.620
I live quite close to the training facility, so that's pretty sweet.

00:11:57.620 --> 00:12:01.360
I don't do a lot of things before I go, I brush my teeth and then I leave.

00:12:01.540 --> 00:12:03.220
And how much do you train?

00:12:03.760 --> 00:12:04.720
That depends.

00:12:06.340 --> 00:12:08.100
How tight the matches are.

00:12:08.260 --> 00:12:10.180
But we try to train every day.

00:12:10.180 --> 00:12:14.220
But sometimes ... Lately, we've gotten a day off after every match.

00:12:14.220 --> 00:12:17.000
And I think that's important, to rest the body but also ...

00:12:17.340 --> 00:12:22.300
... the brain, the mental aspect is also very important. To get away from the football and to get rested.

00:12:22.440 --> 00:12:24.640
How important was that for you, Börje, to rest?

00:12:26.280 --> 00:12:27.660
Yeah ...

00:12:28.920 --> 00:12:32.040
We didn't rest actually, we trained every day.

00:12:32.300 --> 00:12:38.140
But that would also depend, like you say, if we were away on a game and played very well and came home very late ...

00:12:38.140 --> 00:12:39.940
... we would get the next day off.

00:12:40.100 --> 00:12:42.020
But if it hadn't gone well ...

00:12:42.020 --> 00:12:43.820
... and if we had lost, for example ...

00:12:43.820 --> 00:12:45.920
... we would train the morning after.

00:12:45.920 --> 00:12:51.580
But that would depend on what coach we had, a few of our coaches were completely mad in my opinion.

00:12:52.420 --> 00:12:58.340
The first two coaches we had were really good, but then we had a few who were completely ...

00:12:58.340 --> 00:13:00.040
I don't know what to say about them, to be honest.

00:13:00.080 --> 00:13:02.160
They were people who didn't ...

00:13:02.720 --> 00:13:04.640
They weren't like Solskjær?

00:13:04.640 --> 00:13:06.600
They were no good. They were no good.

00:13:06.620 --> 00:13:09.720
They just yelled. They just yelled at the young boys.

00:13:09.800 --> 00:13:14.180
We who were older didn't care, but the younger ones ...

00:13:14.180 --> 00:13:18.520
... they could hardly play. And they barely dared to make a pass at training. And I think that's wrong.

00:13:18.740 --> 00:13:20.660
What do you do when  you relax?

00:13:20.680 --> 00:13:22.280
Yeah, what do I do, Maja?

00:13:22.560 --> 00:13:24.320
What does he do then, Maja?

00:13:25.060 --> 00:13:27.160
He plays PlayStation.

00:13:29.760 --> 00:13:32.360
Or he just lays in our sofa. He just lays there.

00:13:32.360 --> 00:13:33.960
And he watches YouTube.

00:13:33.960 --> 00:13:37.480
But then he will watch PlayStation games on YouTube.

00:13:37.600 --> 00:13:39.640
So it's either or.

00:13:39.680 --> 00:13:40.620
She is exaggerating!

00:13:40.620 --> 00:13:41.440
No, I'm not!

00:13:42.240 --> 00:13:43.260
She is exaggerating!

00:13:43.260 --> 00:13:46.080
So he comes home, sits down in the living room and plays?

00:13:46.240 --> 00:13:47.040
Yeah.

00:13:47.040 --> 00:13:48.560
He has his own room now.

00:13:48.560 --> 00:13:52.380
We had to get him his own room because he was yelling so loud you could hear it all over the house.

00:13:52.380 --> 00:13:53.400
And I needed to work.

00:13:53.400 --> 00:13:54.020
He has a gaming room?!

00:13:54.160 --> 00:13:54.820
Yes.

00:13:54.820 --> 00:13:55.760
Because I needed to work!

00:13:55.760 --> 00:13:58.100
I'm actually very happy with that room, it's become very nice!

00:13:58.280 --> 00:13:59.400
So ...

00:13:59.880 --> 00:14:04.320
I've been happy about that. I need it! I disturb Maja when I play! Or, she says that I do.

00:14:04.320 --> 00:14:08.320
So it's good that I have my own room where I can sit and yell by myself.

00:14:08.320 --> 00:14:09.380
You're having a child.

00:14:09.380 --> 00:14:09.880
Yes.

00:14:09.880 --> 00:14:10.980
And it's not that far ahead.

00:14:11.140 --> 00:14:11.820
No.

00:14:11.820 --> 00:14:12.860
Seven weeks now!

00:14:12.860 --> 00:14:14.620
And then ...

00:14:14.620 --> 00:14:17.780
... the question is, what will happen to this gaming room of his?

00:14:19.820 --> 00:14:23.140
He has asked about that, what it will be like ...

00:14:23.140 --> 00:14:25.100
... as if I have the answer to that, i don't know!

00:14:25.100 --> 00:14:26.600
I have spoken with Maja and asked her if ...

00:14:26.600 --> 00:14:28.760
... if I can spend extra time playing now!

00:14:28.760 --> 00:14:29.880
Before the baby arrives!

00:14:29.880 --> 00:14:31.120
The last weeks!

00:14:31.120 --> 00:14:32.720
Make sure I really play!

00:14:33.000 --> 00:14:35.560
Yes, and there is also this thing with ...

00:14:35.660 --> 00:14:38.300
... sleeping until nine in the morning.

00:14:39.480 --> 00:14:42.760
I make sure I sleep now, because I know that there might not be so much sleep.

00:14:42.760 --> 00:14:44.940
Yes, I think that you should sleep a lot now!

00:14:45.880 --> 00:14:50.200
I have to make sure I sleep now. And I'm very sleepy in the morning.

00:14:50.200 --> 00:14:53.460
So that will be a challenge. But I'm looking forward to it.

00:14:53.460 --> 00:14:54.960
It's very unreal to me.

00:14:55.120 --> 00:14:57.900
But we were at the hospital, and ...

00:14:58.180 --> 00:15:00.300
I got to see the ultrasound.

00:15:00.480 --> 00:15:02.400
And then it became very real.

00:15:02.520 --> 00:15:04.920
It was very moving.

00:15:04.920 --> 00:15:06.860
Were you there during the delivery?

00:15:07.040 --> 00:15:07.900
No.

00:15:07.900 --> 00:15:09.460
I wasn't there for the first one.

00:15:10.480 --> 00:15:12.260
No, it was in Canada.

00:15:12.260 --> 00:15:14.760
The doctor was old fashioned, so they didn't allow me to be there.

00:15:14.780 --> 00:15:17.020
But I was there for the second one.

00:15:17.020 --> 00:15:19.140
Because he was late, and he didn't get there in time.

00:15:19.140 --> 00:15:21.980
Because she was six weeks early.

00:15:21.980 --> 00:15:26.140
And I got there straight from training and just stood there and didn't understand anything.

00:15:26.140 --> 00:15:28.880
I just hurried there fast.

00:15:28.980 --> 00:15:32.720
And I was standing outside, and the nurse came out and said: «What are you standing here for?».

00:15:32.720 --> 00:15:34.980
«Well, I don't know», I said.

00:15:34.980 --> 00:15:39.080
«You should be in there!» she said, and pulled me inside, put clothes on me and I got to be there.

00:15:39.080 --> 00:15:40.740
I was so fucking happy!

00:15:40.740 --> 00:15:42.640
It was fantastic!

00:15:42.900 --> 00:15:44.500
A lot of people say that.

00:15:45.860 --> 00:15:47.760
You didn't faint?

00:15:47.940 --> 00:15:49.340
No. But ...

00:15:49.380 --> 00:15:50.420
I had a lot of ...

00:15:50.640 --> 00:15:53.580
I couldn't complain, but ...

00:15:53.840 --> 00:15:56.320
She almost tore my arm apart!

00:15:56.320 --> 00:15:58.480
But I just had to put on a brave face.

00:15:58.740 --> 00:16:01.800
You can't complain when you're there.

00:16:01.940 --> 00:16:04.020
You just have to be supportive.

00:16:04.020 --> 00:16:06.740
I can imagine that there's a lot of things that I have to look forward to.

00:16:06.740 --> 00:16:07.620
Oh God, yes!

00:16:07.720 --> 00:16:08.540
You do.

00:16:08.760 --> 00:16:11.500
I can vouch for that!

00:16:11.880 --> 00:16:16.880
Good luck, and thank you so much for being here tonight, we're gonna get some more guests in here!

